class Solution {

    static Node deleteAllOccurOfX(Node head, int x) {

        // Pointer used to traverse the DLL
        Node temp = head;

        // Traverse the entire linked list
        while (temp != null) {

            // Store the next node before deleting the current node
            Node front = temp.next;

            // Delete the current node if its value equals x
            if (temp.data == x) {

                // If current node is the head, move head to the next node
                if (temp == head) {
                    head = front;
                }

                // Previous node of current node
                Node back = temp.prev;

                // Connect previous node to next node
                if (back != null) {
                    back.next = front;
                }

                // Connect next node to previous node
                if (front != null) {
                    front.prev = back;
                }
            }

            // Move to the next node
            temp = front;
        }

        return head;
    }
}
Time Complexity: O(n)
Every node is visited exactly once.

Space Complexity:
Auxiliary Space: O(1)

Only three pointers are used:
temp
front
back
No extra data structure is used.
